<h1>Importers</h1>
<p>An importer turns a source file (a PNG, a glTF model, a WAV) into a typed game asset with a stable <code>asset://</code> ID. Importing is how every file gets into a DemiEngine project; cooking later turns those assets into platform-ready data.</p>

<h2>What importing does</h2>
<p>Importing copies or references a source, writes a small <code>*.asset.json</code> manifest next to it, and records a content hash and dependencies. The manifest is the asset's identity — scenes and scripts reference the <code>asset://</code> ID, never the file path. When you edit the source, you reimport and the ID stays the same.</p>
<pre><code>demi asset import assets/textures/skyforge_rune.png \
  --id asset://textures/skyforge_rune</code></pre>
<p><code>demi asset import &lt;source&gt;</code> takes the source file path and <code>--id</code> for the stable <code>asset://</code> identity. It writes a manifest and records the import. If two importers can claim the same file, add <code>--importer &lt;id&gt;</code> to choose.</p>

<h2>Supported sources</h2>
<p>Each importer has an ID (written to the manifest's <code>importer</code> field, or passed via <code>--importer</code> when two importers can claim the same extension):</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Importer ID</th><th>Extensions</th><th>Asset types</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>image</code></td><td>PNG, JPEG, BMP, TGA, QOI</td><td><code>Texture2D</code> and friends</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>svg</code></td><td><code>.svg</code></td><td><code>Icon2D</code>, <code>SvgTexture2D</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>gif</code></td><td><code>.gif</code></td><td><code>GifAnimation2D</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>audio</code></td><td>WAV, OGG, MP3, FLAC</td><td><code>AudioClip</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>font</code></td><td><code>.ttf</code>, <code>.otf</code></td><td><code>Font2D</code>, <code>FontAtlas2D</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>gltf-model</code></td><td><code>.gltf</code>, <code>.glb</code></td><td><code>Model3D</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>model</code></td><td><code>.obj</code>, <code>.iqm</code>, <code>.m3d</code></td><td><code>Model3D</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Video</td><td>MP4, WebM, MOV</td><td><code>VideoClip</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Data</td><td>JSON</td><td><code>DataAsset</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>text</code></td><td><code>.txt</code>, <code>.yaml</code>, <code>.yml</code></td><td><code>Text</code></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>SVG and GIF are separate importers, not flavors of the generic image path: an SVG becomes a vector-sourced <code>Icon2D</code> or <code>SvgTexture2D</code>, and an animated GIF becomes a <code>GifAnimation2D</code>. Each importer's settings live in the manifest (texture filtering, audio streaming, font variations — see <a href="{{ path('docs_page', {slug: 'asset-groups'}) }}">Asset groups &amp; streaming</a> for how they load). The importer ID and version become part of the cook key, so an importer upgrade produces fresh cooked output.</p>

<h2>Working with manifests</h2>
<pre><code>demi asset reimport assets/textures/skyforge_rune.asset.json
demi asset register-generated assets/generated/skyforge_atlas.png
demi asset inspect asset://textures/skyforge_rune
demi asset deps asset://textures/skyforge_rune</code></pre>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>asset reimport &lt;manifest&gt;</code></td><td>Re-runs the import for a changed source: new <code>source_hash</code>, refreshed dependencies and output</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>asset register-generated &lt;source&gt;</code></td><td>Registers a file produced by another tool under <code>assets/</code> so it has a manifest</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>asset inspect &lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Prints the manifest, hash, and dependency summary for an <code>asset://</code> ID</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>asset deps &lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Lists what the asset depends on (textures a model uses, and so on)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>asset collider &lt;…&gt;</code></td><td>Derives collision shape data from a model source</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>asset budget</code></td><td>Reports size and budget figures for project assets</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Run <code>reimport</code> after every source edit. Forgetting it leaves the old hash in place and the cook step will not see the change.</p>

<h2>Carrying assets between projects</h2>
<p>Assets move as a deterministic container with checksums, so both sides can verify nothing changed in transit.</p>
<pre><code>demi asset export-package games/skyforge/packs/skyforge_runes.demipack
demi asset import-package packs/skyforge_runes.demipack</code></pre>
<ul>
  <li><code>asset export-package &lt;out.demipack&gt;</code> — writes a <code>.demipack</code> container: the selected assets plus checksums, in a stable order so two exports of the same content match.</li>
  <li><code>asset import-package &lt;in.demipack&gt;</code> — brings the contents into a project and verifies the checksums.</li>
</ul>
<p>A <code>.demipack</code> is not a full game package — it carries assets, not built games. For installable packages see <a href="{{ path('docs_page', {slug: 'installing-packages'}) }}">Installing packages</a>.</p>

